{"success": true, "message": "Test details sent successfully", "data": {"test": {"_id": "69de21f67e39d99b57bc5b5d", "analysisVideoCdn": "yt", "exam": ["605dfcb2f226ac25a8bd5fef"], "ctype": null, "position": 0, "order": 12, "enableCalculator": false, "isContinuousQuestion": false, "reattemptAvailable": false, "singleSectionMultipleSubjects": false, "timeRestricted": false, "title": "Thermodynamics (C) - Test 4", "description": "Previous Year Questions as Chapter Test", "syllabus": "This test contains questions from all topics of this chapter included in the JEE Main syllabus. It includes a mix of questions from PYQs of JEE Main 2019 - 2025.", "totalTime": 30, "totalQuestions": 20, "totalMarks": 80, "bonusQuestions": null, "bonusMarks": null, "startDate": "2026-04-15T03:30:00.000Z", "endDate": "2027-04-30T00:00:00.000Z", "type": "free", "class": "605df635a37b7025c438d685", "instruction": "608289ffb160b022e9442c83", "subjects": [{"subjectId": "607018ee404ae53194e73d91", "totalMarks": 80, "bonusMarks": 0, "totalQuestions": 20, "bonusQuestions": 0, "_id": "69de4f8d2ee0e063d929bbea"}], "sections": [{"sectionId": {"_id": "69de4f8d2ee0e063d929bba5", "title": "Chemistry Numerical", "sectionType": "normal", "subject": "607018ee404ae53194e73d91", "questions": [{"_id": "69de4f8d2ee0e063d929bb3d", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df8c"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b476e"], "concepts": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b48"], "question": {"text": "<p>An ideal gas undergoes a cyclic transformation starting from the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> and coming back to the same point by tracing the path <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>→</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>→</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>→</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> as shown in the diagram. The total work done in the process is _____<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>.</p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2Ffe267ff1-6e49-4e12-b40d-918c04ed95ac.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 350px; height: 303px;\"/>"}, "options": [{"id": "229e9a", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f8d2ee0e063d929bb3e"}, {"id": "e9ad04", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f8d2ee0e063d929bb3f"}, {"id": "363431", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f8d2ee0e063d929bb40"}, {"id": "a7b98c", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f8d2ee0e063d929bb41"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f8d2ee0e063d929bb42", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df8c"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4783"], "concepts": ["6162fb8d6ed13040ec8503d5"], "question": {"text": "<p>The number of endothermic process/es from the following is _______.</p><p>A. <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>(</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo></math></p><p>B.&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>HCl</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>Cl</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo></math></p><p>C. <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#8594;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo></math></p><p>D. <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>(</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#8594;</mo><msub><mi>CO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>(</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo></math></p><p>E. Dissolution of ammonium chloride in water</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "f303d6", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f8d2ee0e063d929bb43"}, {"id": "a59aab", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f8d2ee0e063d929bb44"}, {"id": "64545d", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f8d2ee0e063d929bb45"}, {"id": "122b60", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f8d2ee0e063d929bb46"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f8d2ee0e063d929bb47", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df8c"], "topics": ["60e2fb2066f9ce3f243b4b70"], "concepts": ["6117b8e067dbe2603c3e8ad2"], "question": {"text": "<p>The standard entropy change for the reaction</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mi>Fe</mi><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfenced><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>Fe</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mn>550</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;at&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>298</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math></p><p>[Given : The standard enthalpy change for the reaction is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mn>165</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kJ</mi><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mol</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>]. The temperature in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math> at which the reaction attains equilibrium is (Nearest Integer)</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "ef25f9", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f8d2ee0e063d929bb48"}, {"id": "65154f", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f8d2ee0e063d929bb49"}, {"id": "b82a1e", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f8d2ee0e063d929bb4a"}, {"id": "a6500d", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f8d2ee0e063d929bb4b"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f8d2ee0e063d929bb4c", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df8c"], "topics": ["60e5671c499d1e49588f8808"], "concepts": ["60e56739499d1e49588f8b61"], "question": {"text": "For the reaction <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>NO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#8652;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>(</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;when <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#916;S</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>176</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#916;H</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>57</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kJ</mi><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mol</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> the magnitude of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#916;G</mi></math> at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>298</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math> for the reaction is _____&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>kJmol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>. (Nearest integer)"}, "options": [{"id": "1dac6b", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f8d2ee0e063d929bb4d"}, {"id": "2167bc", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f8d2ee0e063d929bb4e"}, {"id": "a4c6c9", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f8d2ee0e063d929bb4f"}, {"id": "ae6529", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f8d2ee0e063d929bb50"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f8d2ee0e063d929bb51", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df8c"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b476e"], "concepts": ["60e2fb5666f9ce3f243b4f1a"], "question": {"text": "At constant volume, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi></math> of an ideal gas when heated from <math><mn>300</mn><mi></mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math> to <math><mn>500</mn><mi></mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math> changes its internal energy by <math><mn>5000</mn><mi></mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi><mo>.</mo></math> The molar heat capacity at constant volume is ________"}, "options": [{"id": "6a4310", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f8d2ee0e063d929bb52"}, {"id": "d3b78f", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f8d2ee0e063d929bb53"}, {"id": "3f3155", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f8d2ee0e063d929bb54"}, {"id": "6b6600", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f8d2ee0e063d929bb55"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f8d2ee0e063d929bb56", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df8c"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4783"], "concepts": ["6117b64e478ae845c43c6873"], "question": {"text": "The bond dissociation enthalpy of $\\mathrm{X}_2 \\Delta \\mathrm{H}_{\\text {bond }}$ calculated from the given data is $\\qquad$ $\\mathrm{kJ} \\mathrm{mol}^{-1}$. (Nearest integer)\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& \\mathrm{M}^{+} \\mathrm{X}^{-}(\\mathrm{s}) \\rightarrow \\mathrm{M}^{+}(\\mathrm{g})+\\mathrm{X}^{-}(\\mathrm{g}) \\Delta \\mathrm{H}_{\\text {lattice }}^*=800 \\mathrm{~kJ} \\mathrm{~mol}^{-1} \\\\\n& \\mathrm{M}(\\mathrm{~s}) \\rightarrow \\mathrm{M}(\\mathrm{~g}) \\Delta \\mathrm{H}_{\\text {sub }}^{\\circ}=100 \\mathrm{~kJ} \\mathrm{~mol}^{-1}\n\\end{aligned}$\n$\\mathrm{M}(\\mathrm{~g}) \\rightarrow \\mathrm{M}^{+}(\\mathrm{g})+\\mathrm{e}^{-}(\\mathrm{g}) \\Delta \\mathrm{H}_{\\mathrm{i}}=500 \\mathrm{~kJ} \\mathrm{~mol}^{-1}$\n$\\mathrm{X}(\\mathrm{~g})+\\mathrm{e}^{-}(\\mathrm{g}) \\rightarrow \\mathrm{X}^{-}(\\mathrm{g}) \\Delta \\mathrm{H}_{\\mathrm{eg}}^*=-300 \\mathrm{~kJ} \\mathrm{~mol}^{-1}$\n$\\mathrm{M}(\\mathrm{~s})+\\frac{1}{2} \\mathrm{X}_2(\\mathrm{~g}) \\rightarrow \\mathrm{M}^{+} \\mathrm{X}^{-}(\\mathrm{s}) \\Delta \\mathrm{H}_f^{\\circ}=-400 \\mathrm{~kJ} \\mathrm{~mol}^{-1}$\n[Given : $\\mathrm{M}^{+} \\mathrm{X}^{-}$is a pure ionic compound and X forms a diatomic molecule $\\mathrm{X}_2$ in gaseous state]"}, "options": [{"id": "f8fca0", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f8d2ee0e063d929bb57"}, {"id": "307549", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f8d2ee0e063d929bb58"}, {"id": "202cca", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f8d2ee0e063d929bb59"}, {"id": "8dc6ac", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f8d2ee0e063d929bb5a"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f8d2ee0e063d929bb5b", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df8c"], "topics": ["60e5671c499d1e49588f8808"], "concepts": ["60e5671a499d1e49588f87ea"], "question": {"text": "For the reaction at $298 \\mathrm{~K}, 2 \\mathrm{~A}+\\mathrm{B} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{C} . \\Delta \\mathrm{H}$ $=400 \\mathrm{~kJ} \\mathrm{~mol}^{-1}$ and $\\Delta \\mathrm{S}=0.2 \\mathrm{~kJ} \\mathrm{~mol}^{-1} \\mathrm{~K}^{-1}$. The reaction will become spontaneous above $\\qquad$ K."}, "options": [{"id": "580bbc", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f8d2ee0e063d929bb5c"}, {"id": "62e2a6", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f8d2ee0e063d929bb5d"}, {"id": "d20c38", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f8d2ee0e063d929bb5e"}, {"id": "6c511b", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f8d2ee0e063d929bb5f"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f8d2ee0e063d929bb60", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df8c"], "topics": ["60e2fb2066f9ce3f243b4b70"], "concepts": ["60e2fb9d66f9ce3f243b52d0"], "question": {"text": "<p>One mole of an ideal gas at&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>350</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math> is in a <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi></math> vessel of thermally conducting walls, which are in contact with the surroundings. It undergoes isothermal reversible expansion from&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi></math>&nbsp;to&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi></math> against a constant pressure of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>atm</mi></math>. The change in entropy of the surroundings <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mo>)</mo></math> is _____ <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mrow><mo>&#8211;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> (Nearest integer)</p><p>Given:&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>314</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>.</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "a256ec", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f8d2ee0e063d929bb61"}, {"id": "9d75fd", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f8d2ee0e063d929bb62"}, {"id": "f7de3c", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f8d2ee0e063d929bb63"}, {"id": "f2adad", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f8d2ee0e063d929bb64"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f8d2ee0e063d929bb65", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df8c"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b476e"], "concepts": ["6117b90767dbe2603c3e8fd4"], "question": {"text": "<p>At <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>25</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>50</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> of iron reacts with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>HCl</mi></math> to form <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>FeCl</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>. The evolved hydrogen gas expands against a constant pressure of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>bar</mi></math>. The work done by the gas during this expansion is -_______ <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>.</p><p>(Round off to the Nearest Integer)</p><p>[Given : <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>314</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mol</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>. Assume, hydrogen is an ideal gas]</p><p>[Atomic mass off Fe is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>55</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>85</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">u</mi></math>]</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "e0f5e4", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f8d2ee0e063d929bb66"}, {"id": "8b5935", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f8d2ee0e063d929bb67"}, {"id": "9a3428", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f8d2ee0e063d929bb68"}, {"id": "9fa3b9", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f8d2ee0e063d929bb69"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f8d2ee0e063d929bb6a", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df8c"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4783"], "concepts": ["60e40fd4f1ef260f84ed1e51"], "question": {"text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>17</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math> completely vapourises at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mn>33</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>42</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math>&nbsp;bar pressure and the enthalpy change in the process is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>23</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kJ</mi><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mol</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>. The enthalpy change for the vapourisation of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>85</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math> under the same conditions is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>kJ</mi></math>."}, "options": [{"id": "0c341e", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f8d2ee0e063d929bb6b"}, {"id": "7830c5", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f8d2ee0e063d929bb6c"}, {"id": "269392", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f8d2ee0e063d929b