hML\"><mn>300</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>atm</mi></math> in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Jmol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></math> is (Rounded off to the nearest integer) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>31</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>and</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>ln</mi><mn>10</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>"}, "options": [{"id": "857823", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f8d2ee0e063d929bb75"}, {"id": "889a2b", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f8d2ee0e063d929bb76"}, {"id": "b8f386", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f8d2ee0e063d929bb77"}, {"id": "5f93ff", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f8d2ee0e063d929bb78"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f8d2ee0e063d929bb79", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df8c"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4783"], "concepts": ["60e2fad966f9ce3f243b473a"], "question": {"text": "The formation enthalpies, $\\Delta \\mathrm{H}_{\\mathrm{f}} \\ominus$ for $\\mathrm{H}_{(\\mathrm{g})}$ and $\\mathrm{O}_{(\\mathrm{g})}$ are 220.0 and $250.0 \\mathrm{~kJ} \\mathrm{~mol}^{-1}$, respectively, at 298.15 K , and $\\Delta \\mathrm{H}_{\\mathrm{f}}{ }^{\\ominus}$ for $\\mathrm{H}_2 \\mathrm{O}_{(\\mathrm{g})}$ is $-242.0 \\mathrm{~kJ} \\mathrm{