Correct": null, "_id": "69de4f8d2ee0e063d929bb89"}, {"id": "bcf964", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f8d2ee0e063d929bb8a"}, {"id": "cffb58", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f8d2ee0e063d929bb8b"}, {"id": "8467ac", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f8d2ee0e063d929bb8c"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f8d2ee0e063d929bb8d", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df8c"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b476e"], "concepts": ["6162fb896ed13040ec850101"], "question": {"text": "<p>The molar heat capacity for an ideal gas at constant pressure is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>785</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mol</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>. The change in internal energy is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5000</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math> upon heating it from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>300</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math> to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>500</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math>. The number of moles of the gas at constant volume is____</p><p>(Given: <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>314</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mol</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>)</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "d7c5e3", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f8d2ee0e063d929bb8e"}, {"id": "785324", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f8d2ee0e063d929bb8f"}, {"id": "e27ad8", 